{% comment %}
  OB: brand mark for the rows sharing this treatment (homepage marquee,
  Merken hero chip grid). Cases on the collection handle so an
  Akeneo/Shopify rename falls back to the plain title rather than breaking.

  Renders the brand's real logo file (assets/ob-logo-<handle>.*, sourced from
  each brand's own site - see openspec/changes/refine-homepage-hero-brand-
  logos/logo-sources.json) for every brand one was sourced for. The one
  brand without a usable source logo (Sneaker Lab) falls back to the
  hand-styled wordmark this snippet used before (.ob-logotype / .ob-lt-*,
  ported from mockup/index.html's "Uitgelichte merken" chip treatment, recut
  in Fraunces) so the row never shows a raw collection title. Swap it to a
  real logo by sourcing an asset and moving its handle into the image list
  (.ob-lt-fitflop and friends in component-ob-merken.css stay defined for
  every brand even after its image ships, so this stays a one-line swap).

  Renders an <img> (real logo) or a <span> (fallback) depending on the
  brand - callers must not assume one tag. Size/tint logos via `img`
  descendant selectors on the row's own item class (see
  component-ob-home-marquee.css / component-ob-merken.css's shared
  `.ob-brand-logo` rules), not this snippet - it only picks the asset.

  Optical sizing: a shared height makes a near-square mark (Odlo) tiny and a
  long wordmark (Sweaty Betty, Loewenweiss) huge, so each logo carries a
  `--ob-logo-scale` multiplier the rows apply to their own base height. It is
  equal-visual-weight sizing, derived from the logo's trimmed ink box:
    scale = (4 / ratio)^0.6 * (0.33 / density)^0.3
  where ratio = ink width / height and density = share of that box covered
  by ink (thin serif marks like Pas de Monaco read lighter than dense ones
  like FitFlop at the same size). 4 and 0.33 are the row's "typical" logo.
  Two by-eye corrections on top: FitFlop x0.92, Nike Swim x0.8 (a diagonal
  swoosh reads heavier than its bounding-box density says). Asset files must
  be trimmed to their ink (no transparent padding) or the scale is off - a
  new logo needs trimming and its own scale from the formula above.

  Accepts:
  - collection: {Object} Collection Liquid object (optional if `handle` is given)
  - brand_handle: {String} Brand handle to render, for a brand with no
    collection yet (e.g. RH+ - not synced from Akeneo). Defaults to
    `collection.handle`. Deliberately not named `handle`: Shopify's global
    `handle` (the current page's own handle - "merken" on /pages/merken)
    stays visible inside a rendered snippet, so an omitted `handle` param
    silently resolved to it and every chip fell through to the plain title.
  - style: {String} Pass 'text' to force the hand-styled wordmark treatment
    (.ob-logotype / .ob-lt-*) instead of the real logo image, for a surface
    that deliberately wants styled type over photographic marks (e.g. the
    homepage "Uitgelichte merken" grid, per the mockup's own brand-chip
    treatment). Omit for the default real-logo behavior.

  Usage:
  {% render 'ob-brand-logotype', collection: collection %}
  {% render 'ob-brand-logotype', brand_handle: 'rh-plus' %}
  {% render 'ob-brand-logotype', collection: collection, style: 'text' %}
{% endcomment %}
{%- assign ob_lt_handle = brand_handle | default: collection.handle -%}
{%- if style == 'text' -%}
  {%- case ob_lt_handle -%}
    {%- when 'fitflop' -%}
      <span class="ob-logotype ob-lt-fitflop">fitflop</span>
    {%- when 'hi-tec' -%}
      <span class="ob-logotype ob-lt-hitec">HI-TEC</span>
    {%- when 'holster' -%}
      <span class="ob-logotype ob-lt-holster">holster<small>australia</small></span>
    {%- when 'irasuto-studios' -%}
      <span class="ob-logotype ob-lt-irasuto">Irasuto<small>Studios</small></span>
    {%- when 'juicy-couture' -%}
      <span class="ob-logotype ob-lt-juicy">Juicy Couture</span>
    {%- when 'loewenweiss' -%}
      <span class="ob-logotype ob-lt-loewenweiss">Loewenweiss</span>
    {%- when 'nike-swim' -%}
      <span class="ob-logotype ob-lt-nikeswim">Nike Swim</span>
    {%- when 'odlo' -%}
      <span class="ob-logotype ob-lt-odlo">ODLO</span>
    {%- when 'pas-de-monaco' -%}
      <span class="ob-logotype ob-lt-pasdemonaco">Pas de<small>Monaco</small></span>
    {%- when 'sneaker-lab' -%}
      <span class="ob-logotype ob-lt-sneakerlab">sneaker<b>lab</b></span>
    {%- when 'sweaty-betty' -%}
      <span class="ob-logotype ob-lt-sweatybetty">Sweaty Betty</span>
    {%- else -%}
      <span class="ob-logotype">{{ collection.title }}</span>
  {%- endcase -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- case ob_lt_handle -%}
  {%- when 'fitflop' -%}
    <img
      src="{{ 'ob-logo-fitflop.svg' | asset_url }}"
      alt="FitFlop"
      width="184"
      height="100"
      loading="lazy"
      class="ob-brand-logo"
      style="--ob-logo-scale: 1.25;"
    >
  {%- when 'hi-tec' -%}
    <img
      src="{{ 'ob-logo-hi-tec.png' | asset_url }}"
      alt="Hi-Tec"
      width="290"
      height="54"
      loading="lazy"
      class="ob-brand-logo"
      style="--ob-logo-scale: 0.74;"
    >
  {%- when 'holster' -%}
    <img
      src="{{ 'ob-logo-holster.png' | asset_url }}"
      alt="Holster Australia"
      width="250"
      height="73"
      loading="lazy"
      class="ob-brand-logo"
      style="--ob-logo-scale: 1.28;"
    >
  {%- when 'irasuto-studios' -%}
    <img
      src="{{ 'ob-logo-irasuto-studios.png' | asset_url }}"
      alt="Irasuto Studios"
      width="569"
      height="133"
      loading="lazy"
      class="ob-brand-logo"
      style="--ob-logo-scale: 1.09;"
    >
  {%- when 'juicy-couture' -%}
    <img
      src="{{ 'ob-logo-juicy-couture.png' | asset_url }}"
      alt="Juicy Couture"
      width="599"
      height="102"
      loading="lazy"
      class="ob-brand-logo"
      style="--ob-logo-scale: 0.86;"
    >
  {%- when 'loewenweiss' -%}
    <img
      src="{{ 'ob-logo-loewenweiss.png' | asset_url }}"
      alt="Löwenweiss"
      width="318"
      height="39"
      loading="lazy"
      class="ob-brand-logo"
      style="--ob-logo-scale: 0.71;"
    >
  {%- when 'nike-swim' -%}
    <img
      src="{{ 'ob-logo-nike-swim.png' | asset_url }}"
      alt="Nike Swim"
      width="130"
      height="46"
      loading="lazy"
      class="ob-brand-logo"
      style="--ob-logo-scale: 1.07;"
    >
  {%- when 'odlo' -%}
    <img
      src="{{ 'ob-logo-odlo.svg' | asset_url }}"
      alt="Odlo"
      width="499"
      height="420"
      loading="lazy"
      class="ob-brand-logo"
      style="--ob-logo-scale: 1.75;"
    >
  {%- when 'pas-de-monaco' -%}
    <img
      src="{{ 'ob-logo-pas-de-monaco.png' | asset_url }}"
      alt="Pas de Monaco"
      width="578"
      height="133"
      loading="lazy"
      class="ob-brand-logo"
      style="--ob-logo-scale: 1.35;"
    >
  {%- when 'rh-plus' -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Source file is white text + red bars on transparent (built for the
      brand's own dark navbar) - no dark-on-transparent variant exists, so
      the shared grayscale treatment alone would leave the wordmark
      invisible on this row's light surface. `ob-brand-logo--invert` adds a
      permanent invert (see component-ob-home-marquee.css) instead of the
      usual color-on-hover reveal, which this asset has no legible color
      state for anyway.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <img
      src="{{ 'ob-logo-rh-plus.png' | asset_url }}"
      alt="RH+"
      width="755"
      height="203"
      loading="lazy"
      class="ob-brand-logo ob-brand-logo--invert"
      style="--ob-logo-scale: 1.03;"
    >
  {%- when 'sneaker-lab' -%}
    <span class="ob-logotype ob-lt-sneakerlab">sneaker<b>lab</b></span>
  {%- when 'sweaty-betty' -%}
    <img
      src="{{ 'ob-logo-sweaty-betty.svg' | asset_url }}"
      alt="Sweaty Betty"
      width="1306"
      height="122"
      loading="lazy"
      class="ob-brand-logo"
      style="--ob-logo-scale: 0.52;"
    >
  {%- else -%}
    <span class="ob-logotype">{{ collection.title }}</span>
{%- endcase -%}
{%- endif -%}
